The name section's function and global maps in index order.

A name map lists its entries by increasing index (the name section's
appendix), and TeaVM writes each in the order of its collection, where an
imported function or global may come after defined ones, though the index
space numbers imports first.  Out of order, a map is not one the appendix
allows: wasm-tools names nothing from its first entry out of order on, and
warmc ignores the section.  The other maps list collections whose order is
their index order already.

test/teavm/fixes: every program's module, its maps checked in run_teavm.py.

